+# 72a6d8b343e4 — Endpoint Bridge
 
-0-bg grid (h~5-7, w~7-9) with 1-3 PAIRS of cells in distinct non-bg colors. Each pair is AXIALLY ALIGNED — the two cells share the same row (horizontal pair) OR the same column (vertical pair) — with at least one empty cell between them. The cells between the pair are 0. Rule: for every color appearing in EXACTLY 2 cells that share a row OR column, DRAW a STRAIGHT LINE connecting the two cells in that color: fill all cells between (and including) the two endpoints in the row/col with the color. Pairs not axially aligned are ignored. Net: each axially-aligned same-color pair becomes a continuous colored line spanning its axis.
+Version `3.0.0` generates sparse `0`-background grids in which a nonzero color is bridged only when it appears **exactly twice** and the two cells share a row or column. The inclusive row/column span is filled; diagonal pairs, singletons, adjacent pairs, and aligned three-occurrence colors remain unchanged.
 
-Kind: `per_puzzle`. Imported version: `2.0.1`.
-Approval is derived by the catalog from current code and retained evidence.
+The distribution now mixes positive horizontal/vertical bridges with two explicit negative families: diagonal exact pairs refute “connect every pair,” and aligned triples refute “connect aligned occurrences regardless of multiplicity.” Reserved, disjoint footprints prevent accidental crossings or overwrites from changing the lesson.
+
+Public exact controls are `grid_h`, `grid_w`, `n_horizontal`, `n_vertical`, `n_diagonal`, `n_triples`, `n_singletons`, and `n_adjacent`. Every advertised value is observable and valid in every difficulty band. Unknown or out-of-range controls are rejected.
+
+One deterministic slot in each three-sample block uses a canonical-size/palette profile; other samples emphasize shortcut witnesses. `RULE_HASH = "3650a4704dc3"` pins the unchanged canonical Racket authority. Approval remains catalog-derived.
